                <pb facs="0371" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3906: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sevier</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-14T15:00:00-04:00">July 14, 1934—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>55. Your 59, July 9, 6 p.m. You may wish to say to Cruchaga that Assistant
                    Secretary Welles took occasion to mention to the Paraguayan Minister that we
                    have been informed both from Santiago and by the Chilean Minister here of the
                    deep concern with which the Chilean Government views the friction now existing
                    between Chile and Paraguay, and expressed our hope that no break in relations
                    might take place.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
